Stay quiet about a device that is gone

razerkbd, razermouse and razeraccessory try a failed request five times,
10 ms apart, and log two lines each time. A device that has been
unplugged fails every one of them with -ENODEV, so an app that draws on
it gets about ten kernel lines and 50 ms of waiting for every frame.
Return -ENODEV at once, and don't log it in the send and receive
functions either.

Applies to OpenRazer master (f5d547093d30fb2efa9c57469a1a30a0a1a279a5) after 0001 and 0002.

diff --git a/driver/razeraccessory_driver.c b/driver/razeraccessory_driver.c
index ecb7c6e..24faf76 100644
--- a/driver/razeraccessory_driver.c
+++ b/driver/razeraccessory_driver.c
@@ -62,6 +62,9 @@ static int __must_check razer_send_payload(struct razer_accessory_device *device
         err = razer_get_report(device->hdev, request, response);
         mutex_unlock(&device->lock);
         if (err) {
+            /* A device that is gone fails every try, and saying so each time fills the log */
+            if (err == -ENODEV)
+                return err;
             print_erroneous_report(device->hdev, response, "Invalid Report Length");
             goto retry;
         }
